# What must never be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# BELT AND BRACES, NOT LOAD-BEARING. Every path below is already covered by
# .gitignore, and the Vercel CLI falls back to .gitignore when this file is
# absent — so nothing here changes what gets deployed today. It exists to make
# the exclusion explicit and to stop it depending on .gitignore continuing to
# be correct: the two files answer different questions ("what do we version?"
# versus "what do we ship?"), and they only happen to agree right now.
#
# The paths matter because `public/images` and `public/videos` hold 434 MB of
# local working media — full-resolution stock originals, none of it committed
# and none of it referenced by any working code path. Git-triggered deploys
# build from the repository and have never seen it. A `vercel --prod` from a
# developer's machine uploads the working DIRECTORY instead, so the day
# somebody loosens a .gitignore rule, this is what stops half a gigabyte of
# unused media becoming a public URL on a project whose users are on metered
# mobile data.

public/images
public/videos

# Local-only working files: audit output, Playwright snapshots, scratch scripts.
audit
.playwright-mcp
scripts/tmp
